# ============================================================
# Windows Password Spraying Detection
# ============================================================
#
# SOC L1 Detection | Splunk | Windows Security Event Logs
#
# Objective:
# Detect potential password spraying activity by identifying
# a single source IP attempting authentication against
# multiple user accounts.
#
# Password spraying pattern:
# One source IP -> Multiple users -> Failed logons
#
# Event ID:
# 4625 - Failed logon
#
# Detection threshold:
# 5 or more unique user accounts targeted by the same
# source IP.
#
# ============================================================


# 1. Detection Query
# ------------------------------------------------------------

index=* signature_id=4625
| stats dc(user) as unique_users count as failed_attempts by src_ip
| where unique_users >= 5
| sort - unique_users


# ============================================================
# 2. Query Explanation
# ============================================================
#
# index=* signature_id=4625
# Searches Windows failed authentication events.
#
# stats dc(user) as unique_users
# Counts the number of unique user accounts targeted by
# each source IP.
#
# count as failed_attempts
# Counts the total number of failed authentication attempts
# from each source IP.
#
# by src_ip
# Groups the results by source IP address.
#
# where unique_users >= 5
# Filters for source IPs targeting five or more unique users.
#
# sort - unique_users
# Displays source IPs targeting the largest number of users
# first.
#
# ============================================================


# 3. Detection Result
# ============================================================
#
# The detection identified suspicious authentication activity
# associated with:
#
# Source IP: 91.219.237.15
# Unique users targeted: 15
# Failed authentication attempts: 30
# Detection threshold: 5+ unique users
#
# Assessment:
# Potential Windows password spraying activity.
#
# ============================================================


# 4. SOC L1 Investigation Trigger
# ============================================================
#
# When the detection triggers:
#
# - Identify the suspicious source IP.
# - Identify all targeted user accounts.
# - Review the number and timing of failed attempts.
# - Check for successful authentication (Event ID 4624).
# - Review suspicious activity following authentication.
# - Determine whether the source IP appears on other systems.
# - Escalate if additional suspicious activity is identified.
#
# ============================================================
# End of Password Spraying Detection
# ============================================================
